.TH BTRFS-SNAPMAN-CLI 1 "November 2026" "btrfs-snapman 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
btrfs-snapman-cli \- terminal manager for btrfs subvolume snapshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B btrfs-snapman-cli
.br
.B btrfs-snapman-cli
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-color ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B btrfs-snapman-cli
is the terminal front end of btrfs-snapman, for SSH sessions and headless
machines.
It does everything the GTK interface,
.BR btrfs-snapman (1),
does, through the same root helpers and configuration.
.PP
Without a command, on a terminal, it opens a full-screen interface: volumes on
the left, the selected volume's snapshots on the right, and the command log
below.
Press
.B ?
for the keys.
It needs at least 80\(mu24 characters.
.PP
With a command, it does one operation and exits, for scripts and cron.
Results go to standard output; the equivalent shell commands (\fB$ ...\fR),
notes, hook output and warnings go to standard error.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR list " [\fIvolume\fR]"
Without
.IR volume :
one line per volume with its path and snapshot count
.RB ( ! ,
followed by the error, if it can't be read).
With
.IR volume :
its snapshots, newest first, with creation time, age, RO or RW, and the flags
.BR received ,
.B mounted
and
.BR "not from this source" .
.TP
.B locations
The approved locations for new volumes: path, snapshot root, and the file that
defines it.
.TP
.BR snapshot " \fIvolume\fR [\fIcomment\fR] [" \-\-ro | \-\-rw ]
Take a snapshot and print its name.
In the comment, spaces become underscores and only letters, digits,
.B _
and
.B \-
are kept.
Read-only or not follows the volume's setting unless given.
.TP
.BR delete " \fIvolume snapshot\fR [" \-\-yes ]
Delete a snapshot.
On a terminal, type
.B delete
to confirm; otherwise
.B \-\-yes
is required.
.TP
.BR set\-ro " \fIvolume snapshot\fR " on | off " [" \-\-force ]
Make a snapshot read-only or writable.
Making a snapshot created by
.B btrfs receive
writable breaks incremental send chains: on a terminal you are asked to
confirm; otherwise
.B \-\-force
is required.
.TP
.BR new\-volume " \fIname parent\fR [" \-\-folder " \fIf\fR] [" \-\-nocow | \-\-existing ]
Create a subvolume
.IR parent / f
(default: the name) and its snapshot folder, and register it.
.I parent
must be an approved location.
.B \-\-existing
registers a subvolume that is already there.
.TP
.BR remove\-volume " \fIname\fR [" \-\-delete\-data " [" \-\-no\-final\-snapshot | \-\-delete\-snapshots "]] [" \-\-yes ]
Unregister a volume created by btrfs-snapman.
With
.BR \-\-delete\-data ,
also delete the subvolume, after taking a final read-only snapshot unless told
otherwise.
Prints what will happen, then asks you to type the volume name (or needs
.BR \-\-yes ).
.TP
.BR add\-location " \fIpath\fR [" \-\-snapshot\-root " \fIdir\fR]"
Approve a folder on btrfs for new volumes.
Their snapshots go in
.I dir
(default:
.I snapshots
at the top of the same filesystem).
.TP
.BR remove\-location " \fIpath\fR [" \-\-yes ]
Withdraw an approved location.
Volumes already there stay registered.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print each root helper's JSON object unchanged, instead of the usual output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
No colour.
Also when the
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable is set, or when standard output is not a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH PRIVILEGES
The program runs as the calling user and reaches the root helpers in
.I /usr/libexec/btrfs-snapman
with
.BR "sudo \-n" ,
or directly when already root.
When sudo needs a password,
.B sudo \-v
asks for it on the terminal (outside the full-screen interface) and the call
is retried once.
Listing and snapshot changes use the sudo timestamp; creating or removing a
volume, or approving or withdrawing a location, asks for the password every
time.
Without a terminal nothing can be asked, so unattended use needs root or a
sudoers rule; see
.IR /usr/share/doc/btrfs-snapman-cli/examples/sudoers.example .
The password is never read, stored or passed on by the program.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The helper refused or failed; its error is printed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
sudo authentication failed or was cancelled.
.TP
.B 4
Not confirmed, or confirmation needed without a terminal and no
.B \-\-yes
or
.BR \-\-force .
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH EXAMPLES
Snapshot before an upgrade, from a script:
.PP
.RS
.nf
btrfs\-snapman\-cli snapshot Docker "before pihole v6"
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/btrfs-snapman/
Configuration, shared with
.BR btrfs-snapman (1).
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/btrfs-snapman-cli/examples/sudoers.example
Example sudo rules, e.g. listing without a password.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR btrfs-snapman (1),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR visudo (8),
.BR btrfs-subvolume (8)
.PP
Changes are logged to the journal: \fBjournalctl \-t btrfs-snapman\fR.
